          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which conditions covered here have a three-character code that takes no further character?",
          "answer": "Based on the coding documents I searched, one condition in the set fits this description: **essential (primary) hypertension, code I10**. The source is \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family.\" It says I10 \"takes none\" of the further characters that most categories need, so it is a complete code at three characters.\n\nThe other conditions in the results do not qualify, according to the same sources:\n- **Type 2 diabetes (E11)** is a category that is subdivided further. The example in the results, E11.9, has extra characters. Source: \"Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories.\"\n- **COPD (J44)** uses its fourth character to show whether a complication is present. Source: \"Coding chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: J44 and its two complication codes.\"\n\nThe results did not cover every condition in the coding system. So this answer covers only the conditions the search returned, not a complete list. These are coding rules, not medical guidance about any person's health.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
